{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T19:40:15.287Z","data":{"text":"Both verifies pass. Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Task 2 of change 169-slice-registries** — \"When a slice names a command, createProgram registers it and the root help lists it in its declared group\" — is done.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **`src/cli/help-groups.ts`**: new exported `commandGroups(slices)` returning fresh arrays (a `COMMAND_GROUPS` command keeps its place when the slice declares that group, else throws `slice <slice>: command <name> is listed under <title>, not <group>`; any other command appends to its declared group in registry order), `configureGroupedHelp(program, groups)` now formats the root help from the passed `groups`, and new `registerSliceCommands(program, slices)` with both checks and exact messages.\n- **`src/cli/index.ts`**: `createProgram(version?, slices = SLICES)` registers slice commands after its own commands and installs the grouped root help via `commandGroups(slices)`. The file sits exactly at the 250-line budget; `createProgram` stays over 80 lines so its function-budget grandfather entry holds.\n- **`tests/help-groups.test.ts`**: the \"names exactly the registered commands\" test now uses `commandGroups(SLICES)`; all other tests unchanged (`tests.modify: true` set).\n- **`tests/cli-slice-commands.test.ts`** (new): proves the \"Slice commands\" scenarios — the full \"placed by group\" table, the join-the-group and default-help behavior, and both clash/missing rows with exact messages.\n- Result written to `.run/results/2.md`.\n\n`pnpm verify` (proposal verify) exits 0; the task's verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/cli-slice-commands.test.ts`) passes 10/10."}}
